WEBVTT

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:34.940
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:01:31.530 --> 00:01:33.200
Halloween!

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:39.620
I just can't deal with autumn.

00:01:40.110 --> 00:01:42.700
I get really depressed.

00:01:43.270 --> 00:01:44.020
Really?

00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:48.010
When the sun doesn't shine as much, 
and the north wind starts blowing...

00:01:48.330 --> 00:01:51.320
I get excited about the 
fact that it's getting cold.

00:01:51.830 --> 00:01:55.030
Wouldn't you usually think about 
how fleeting everything is?

00:01:55.030 --> 00:01:56.990
You're the only one that's happy.

00:01:58.420 --> 00:02:00.310
Hey, did you know?

00:02:00.310 --> 00:02:02.740
You're gonna be really excited!

00:02:02.740 --> 00:02:04.850
And there's another one.

00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:09.400
What are you so excited about, Panda?

00:02:10.110 --> 00:02:12.320
You'll get candy!

00:02:12.890 --> 00:02:13.830
Who'll get candy?

00:02:14.620 --> 00:02:16.400
Me, I think.

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:17.530
And who'll give you candy?

00:02:18.160 --> 00:02:19.910
I wonder who it'll be?

00:02:20.670 --> 00:02:23.530
May I end this conversation?

00:02:24.160 --> 00:02:25.520
I'm trying to tell you

00:02:25.520 --> 00:02:28.310
that today is a day you get candy.

00:02:28.310 --> 00:02:30.400
Are you referring to Halloween?

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:32.200
Yeah, that's it!

00:02:32.200 --> 00:02:33.960
I'm amazed you were able to get that

00:02:33.960 --> 00:02:35.590
from this vague explanation.

00:02:36.220 --> 00:02:39.550
We have Halloween 
decorations up, as well.

00:02:44.240 --> 00:02:45.110
See?

00:02:45.110 --> 00:02:46.430
Oh, that's why.

00:02:47.070 --> 00:02:48.260
I thought you had joined

00:02:48.260 --> 00:02:51.480
the Friends-with-pumpkins 
group, Miss Sasako.

00:02:52.910 --> 00:02:54.440
And why is that?

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:57.400
Well, you know...

00:02:58.740 --> 00:03:00.400
Why is that?

00:03:01.140 --> 00:03:02.470
Never mind.

00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:06.010
Let's stop right there, Miss Sasako.

00:03:06.970 --> 00:03:11.290
Whatever. Let's just 
hurry and go get candy!

00:03:11.290 --> 00:03:14.340
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:03:15.160 --> 00:03:17.380
Mr. Penguin, Mr. Penguin.

00:03:17.380 --> 00:03:19.050
What is it, Panda?

00:03:19.880 --> 00:03:23.000
You look really good 
in that, Mr. Penguin.

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:23.760
Really?

00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:26.230
What a cute looking scrubbing brush.

00:03:27.290 --> 00:03:29.240
I'm supposed to be a 
baby king penguin!

00:03:29.240 --> 00:03:31.210
It's puffy, isn't it?

00:03:31.210 --> 00:03:33.140
Mr. Penguin, Mr. Penguin.

00:03:33.770 --> 00:03:35.480
What is it, Polar Bear?

00:03:35.690 --> 00:03:39.300
Should I have worn pants after all?

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:42.200
I don't think that really matters...

00:03:45.160 --> 00:03:48.010
Give us some candy, Mr. Grizzly!

00:03:48.010 --> 00:03:49.370
Give! Give!

00:03:50.700 --> 00:03:52.330
Why the hell would I?

00:03:52.690 --> 00:03:54.300
The reason's not important!

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:56.300
Just give us candy!

00:03:56.630 --> 00:03:58.110
This is a bar.

00:03:58.650 --> 00:04:01.330
Why would we have candy or gum?

00:04:01.330 --> 00:04:04.590
Then we'll settle for your bank book.

00:04:04.930 --> 00:04:06.260
Like I'd give that to you!

00:04:08.380 --> 00:04:09.680
Here.

00:04:10.210 --> 00:04:13.140
Beef jerky? That's rather stoic.

00:04:14.980 --> 00:04:17.560
Thank you, Mr. Grizzly.

00:04:18.500 --> 00:04:20.120
S-Sure.

00:04:20.120 --> 00:04:21.860
Thank you, my dear Grizzly.

00:04:22.740 --> 00:04:24.530
You need to stop!

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:28.030
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:04:28.030 --> 00:04:31.500
Toraya

00:04:29.350 --> 00:04:31.500
Give us candy, please!

00:04:32.230 --> 00:04:33.410
What'll it be?

00:04:33.900 --> 00:04:36.400
What? We can choose anything?

00:04:37.630 --> 00:04:39.360
I wonder what I should pick?

00:04:39.360 --> 00:04:40.420
I'll take this.

00:04:41.270 --> 00:04:42.630
Smelt mochi coming right up!

00:04:43.120 --> 00:04:46.390
I want these things 
that look like paws.

00:04:47.240 --> 00:04:48.550
Sweet paws coming right up!

00:04:49.300 --> 00:04:50.890
Will this all be on one check?

00:04:51.630 --> 00:04:52.220
Huh?

00:04:52.220 --> 00:04:55.770
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:04:57.470 --> 00:04:59.730
Who knew we'd have to pay.

00:05:00.230 --> 00:05:02.840
I apparently wasn't thinking.

00:05:02.840 --> 00:05:05.770
It's only obvious that we'd have 
to pay for something in a store.

00:05:10.400 --> 00:05:12.390
The red bean filling is delicious.

00:05:12.390 --> 00:05:14.250
Maybe I should serve something

00:05:14.250 --> 00:05:15.150
with red bean at the café.

00:05:15.150 --> 00:05:16.370
Polar Bear!

00:05:17.840 --> 00:05:19.110
Just kidding.

00:05:19.110 --> 00:05:20.240
Jeez.

00:05:20.940 --> 00:05:23.310
More importantly, aren't you 
excessively changing costumes?

00:05:23.310 --> 00:05:25.090
Where are you even changing?

00:05:28.220 --> 00:05:29.840
In a dark alley?

00:05:30.280 --> 00:05:32.280
Working hard, aren't you?

00:05:33.770 --> 00:05:36.120
It's your nephew and his friend.

00:05:37.380 --> 00:05:39.250
Good evening.

00:05:39.250 --> 00:05:42.350
Wow, you've got quite 
a bit of candy there.

00:05:42.350 --> 00:05:43.780
Let's see...

00:05:44.170 --> 00:05:46.450
Here you go, Uncle. For you.

00:05:47.860 --> 00:05:49.320
Thank you.

00:05:53.450 --> 00:05:56.230
Sorry, could you not 
stare at me like that?

00:05:59.140 --> 00:06:01.490
Um... puffy?

00:06:03.940 --> 00:06:05.800
Bye-bye!

00:06:08.970 --> 00:06:12.290
I wonder why I even 
picked this costume.

00:06:12.800 --> 00:06:14.890
This is a lot of candy.

00:06:15.470 --> 00:06:17.900
I wonder what's so different 
between us and them?

00:06:17.900 --> 00:06:19.860
Probably the level of cuteness?

00:06:19.860 --> 00:06:23.560
But my cuteness is 
unprecedented, too, isn't it?

00:06:23.560 --> 00:06:27.030
Their cuteness is unconscious 
and free of wicked thoughts.

00:06:27.530 --> 00:06:28.880
All right!

00:06:28.880 --> 00:06:31.120
I'll work on making my 
cuteness unconscious,

00:06:31.120 --> 00:06:34.030
so I can get more candy!

00:06:34.830 --> 00:06:37.040
Wicked thoughts everywhere.

00:06:38.010 --> 00:06:38.910
Uh oh.

00:06:40.120 --> 00:06:42.960
Whatcha doin', Polar Bear?

00:06:42.960 --> 00:06:46.460
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:06:47.610 --> 00:06:48.880
Please, help yourself.

00:06:49.680 --> 00:06:51.840
Take whatever you'd like.

00:06:53.250 --> 00:06:55.810
I appreciate the thought, but...

00:06:56.560 --> 00:06:59.280
I put a lot of effort 
into these bonsai.

00:06:59.280 --> 00:07:01.870
This is a great opportunity, 
so I'll let you borrow some.

00:07:02.520 --> 00:07:04.480
This is a little too deep for me...

00:07:04.950 --> 00:07:06.980
If I had to choose...

00:07:08.760 --> 00:07:09.490
How about this one?

00:07:09.930 --> 00:07:12.100
Oh, one moment.

00:07:12.100 --> 00:07:13.870
The branches need a little work.

00:07:20.630 --> 00:07:23.130
This shape is indescribable.

00:07:23.700 --> 00:07:24.950
How about it?

00:07:24.950 --> 00:07:27.660
Would you all like to 
prune them, as well?

00:07:27.660 --> 00:07:30.290
No, not today.

00:07:30.550 --> 00:07:40.600
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:07:42.620 --> 00:07:43.980
Leave it to me!

00:07:44.530 --> 00:07:47.170
Okay! I want lots!

00:07:47.170 --> 00:07:48.900
Really, Anteater?

00:07:49.470 --> 00:07:52.400
There's just about 5,000 
of them wriggling about!

00:07:55.620 --> 00:07:56.870
Never mind.

00:07:56.870 --> 00:07:58.000
You sure?

00:07:58.000 --> 00:07:59.210
Oh, I know!

00:08:01.160 --> 00:08:03.670
We have white ones, too!

00:08:04.050 --> 00:08:05.550
Not a chance!

00:08:08.100 --> 00:08:09.920
Coffee in a can, huh?

00:08:10.800 --> 00:08:12.880
At least it's not wriggling about.

00:08:13.580 --> 00:08:14.530
Did you know?

00:08:15.170 --> 00:08:17.840
The calories in a can of coffee

00:08:17.840 --> 00:08:21.060
is equal to about 1,800 ants.

00:08:21.600 --> 00:08:23.600
Could you not explain it that way?

00:08:24.480 --> 00:08:27.940
Hal... lo... ween?

00:08:27.940 --> 00:08:30.280
That's right, Tortoise.

00:08:33.290 --> 00:08:35.950
I'll go get some now.

00:08:36.600 --> 00:08:39.740
Ice cream!

00:08:40.040 --> 00:08:40.910
Huh?

00:08:41.520 --> 00:08:44.210
Heave-ho!

00:08:44.210 --> 00:08:46.730
Um, Tortoise?

00:08:44.620 --> 00:08:46.730
Heave-ho!

00:08:49.130 --> 00:08:50.550
You know,

00:08:51.040 --> 00:08:53.470
this isn't really ice cream, but rather...

00:08:53.470 --> 00:08:54.700
...ice soup?

00:08:57.050 --> 00:09:00.560
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:09:00.560 --> 00:09:03.520
Please, please, come in!

00:09:04.040 --> 00:09:06.440
Close, close, way too close.

00:09:06.720 --> 00:09:09.440
Please, please. 
It's not much, but...

00:09:10.040 --> 00:09:11.590
Close, too close.

00:09:11.590 --> 00:09:14.400
Making pickles has 
been my hobby lately.

00:09:14.400 --> 00:09:17.910
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:09:21.350 --> 00:09:22.880
We've got quite the haul.

00:09:22.880 --> 00:09:25.270
But I want candy...

00:09:25.270 --> 00:09:26.840
This isn't right, is it?

00:09:26.840 --> 00:09:28.610
We can't really call this 
Halloween, can we?

00:09:28.610 --> 00:09:30.900
Yay! Yay!

00:09:30.900 --> 00:09:33.310
My, today is a wonderful day.

00:09:32.590 --> 00:09:33.310
Yay!

00:09:33.310 --> 00:09:35.110
It sure is.

00:09:35.110 --> 00:09:38.500
To think we got free items 
everywhere we went.

00:09:38.500 --> 00:09:41.230
I got all this!

00:09:41.230 --> 00:09:43.330
Halloween is a wonderful day.

00:09:43.330 --> 00:09:45.680
So economical!

00:09:45.680 --> 00:09:48.980
I wonder what they're going for.

00:09:49.530 --> 00:09:53.120
Should we go back and try to 
exchange this for candy?

00:09:53.570 --> 00:09:55.110
How about the opposite?

00:09:56.090 --> 00:09:58.660
Instead of receiving, 
why don't we try giving?

00:09:59.520 --> 00:10:00.640
Giving?

00:10:05.060 --> 00:10:08.040
Oh? You didn't get anything?

00:10:08.420 --> 00:10:10.420
We received, and then...

00:10:10.420 --> 00:10:11.680
...we gave it away.

00:10:12.190 --> 00:10:14.000
We did something really good.

00:10:18.720 --> 00:10:20.350
What the heck is all this?

00:10:24.060 --> 00:10:29.560
To Mr. Handa,
This is for you.
From Sasako

00:10:24.060 --> 00:10:29.560
Bonsai

00:10:25.150 --> 00:10:26.920
"To Mr. Handa,

00:10:26.920 --> 00:10:28.350
This is for you.

00:10:28.350 --> 00:10:29.560
From Sasako."

00:10:31.420 --> 00:10:32.970
I see. It's from Panda.

00:10:34.370 --> 00:10:37.640
I bet Mr. Handa's really happy.

00:10:37.640 --> 00:10:38.940
Yeah, well...

00:10:38.940 --> 00:10:41.290
He probably didn't need the receipt.

00:10:43.410 --> 00:10:52.960
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:10:52.960 --> 00:10:57.880
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:10:54.960 --> 00:10:56.950
Llama Day!

00:11:01.410 --> 00:11:03.350
I'm a little tired, 
but it was a lot of fun.

00:11:03.980 --> 00:11:05.650
It's good that we 
got to see everything.

00:11:06.860 --> 00:11:08.300
But you didn't.

00:11:09.700 --> 00:11:13.170
You didn't visit the Llama Corner.

00:11:13.680 --> 00:11:15.940
Even now, you're trying to pass by.

00:11:16.350 --> 00:11:17.190
Huh?

00:11:18.230 --> 00:11:19.230
Oh, a llama.

00:11:19.720 --> 00:11:20.540
Yes.

00:11:23.410 --> 00:11:25.740
I'd like to establish a Llama Day.

00:11:25.740 --> 00:11:33.710
Request to Establish Llama Day

00:11:27.320 --> 00:11:30.330
What's this "Llama Day"?

00:11:30.330 --> 00:11:31.560
It's a day for llamas.

00:11:32.260 --> 00:11:33.710
A day for llamas?

00:11:34.900 --> 00:11:38.130
A day for llamas, 
made by llamas for llamas.

00:11:40.260 --> 00:11:41.550
Um...

00:11:41.830 --> 00:11:44.490
Why are we creating a Llama Day?

00:11:44.490 --> 00:11:48.600
Because I feel that llamas are 
being treated too apathetically.

00:11:49.230 --> 00:11:50.600
Apathetically <i>(ozanari)</i>?

00:11:53.320 --> 00:11:55.060
Delicious!

00:11:55.060 --> 00:11:56.440
That would be a rice ball <i>(onigiri)</i>.

00:11:59.050 --> 00:12:00.140
Delicious!

00:12:00.670 --> 00:12:02.150
That would be oinari sushi.

00:12:04.830 --> 00:12:07.790
Delicious...

00:12:06.410 --> 00:12:07.790
That would be a sunflower <i>(himawari)</i>.

00:12:08.140 --> 00:12:10.160
Apa-the-ti-cal-ly.

00:12:10.800 --> 00:12:12.730
I guess he means that the customers

00:12:12.730 --> 00:12:14.960
don't pay much attention to him.

00:12:15.520 --> 00:12:18.420
Were you that unpopular, Mr. Llama?

00:12:18.790 --> 00:12:21.010
That's because you're 
so dull, Mr. Llama.

00:12:21.770 --> 00:12:24.340
Thank you for your honest opinion.

00:12:24.850 --> 00:12:26.590
Come to think of it,

00:12:26.590 --> 00:12:29.100
where are you located 
in the zoo, Mr. Llama?

00:12:29.510 --> 00:12:31.840
Right next to the Panda Corner.

00:12:32.390 --> 00:12:36.000
No! I think it's by the restaurant.

00:12:32.390 --> 00:12:36.270
Restaurant

00:12:37.080 --> 00:12:39.490
No, no. It's right by the back gate.

00:12:41.300 --> 00:12:43.540
Where...?

00:12:44.110 --> 00:12:44.980
Right here.

00:12:46.140 --> 00:12:48.270
He's right next to Mr. Giraffe.

00:12:48.270 --> 00:12:50.200
Why don't any of you remember?

00:12:52.360 --> 00:12:55.000
Problem solved! 
Thanks for all your hard work!

00:12:55.730 --> 00:12:57.520
Oh, thank goodness.

00:12:57.520 --> 00:13:01.700
Um, we weren't talking about 
where the Llama Corner is...

00:13:03.840 --> 00:13:06.120
Let us continue the meeting.

00:13:06.120 --> 00:13:06.900
Here.

00:13:07.380 --> 00:13:08.970
Go ahead, Mr. Tapir.

00:13:09.320 --> 00:13:11.770
Perhaps no one visits you because they

00:13:11.770 --> 00:13:13.930
don't know where you're located.

00:13:13.930 --> 00:13:15.480
Why don't you put up a sign?

00:13:16.170 --> 00:13:17.600
That's a good idea.

00:13:18.900 --> 00:13:21.030
Llama 
<— 
This Way

00:13:18.900 --> 00:13:21.030
Llama 50m                 Llama 55m                Llama 60m                      Llama 65m                Llama 70m
away.                          away.                        away.                              away.                         away.

00:13:21.150 --> 00:13:23.610
Almost                                                                  Almost
to the                                                                    to the
Llama.                                                                  Llama.

00:13:21.150 --> 00:13:23.610
Llama is          Llama Over      Llama is                   Llama Over    Llama is      Llama Over
Present.          There.               Present.                    There.            Present.       There.

00:13:23.490 --> 00:13:25.860
Llama Over Here.

00:13:23.490 --> 00:13:25.860
Llama!

00:13:23.650 --> 00:13:25.860
Llama is present.

00:13:23.650 --> 00:13:25.860
Did you see 
the llama?

00:13:23.650 --> 00:13:25.860
Llama 
100 M 
away.

00:13:26.220 --> 00:13:27.360
Um...

00:13:27.360 --> 00:13:30.240
Wouldn't it look like you 
were the only one at our zoo?

00:13:30.240 --> 00:13:31.560
What a wonderful idea,

00:13:31.560 --> 00:13:33.370
a zoo with just me.

00:13:33.370 --> 00:13:35.080
I don't think that'll work...

00:13:35.470 --> 00:13:36.710
That sounds great!

00:13:36.710 --> 00:13:39.390
That means everyone else would be off!

00:13:39.390 --> 00:13:42.530
But then no one might come.

00:13:42.530 --> 00:13:44.390
Good point.

00:13:45.310 --> 00:13:49.050
Thank you for your brutally 
honest opinion.

00:13:49.700 --> 00:13:52.680
I think it's better if we 
have a lot of animals.

00:13:52.680 --> 00:13:55.730
Then how about everyone 
becomes a llama?

00:14:01.270 --> 00:14:03.730
Aren't I cute as a llama?

00:14:04.250 --> 00:14:07.160
Your llama is great, 
too, Mr. Tortoise!

00:14:07.610 --> 00:14:10.330
Really...?

00:14:10.330 --> 00:14:11.910
I don't see the point in you wearing

00:14:11.910 --> 00:14:13.400
a llama costume, Mr. Llama.

00:14:14.730 --> 00:14:17.810
Do you have a sales point, Mr. Llama?

00:14:18.690 --> 00:14:19.630
Oh!

00:14:19.630 --> 00:14:20.630
What is it, Mr. Llama?

00:14:21.460 --> 00:14:24.510
I have an interest in bonsai.

00:14:26.750 --> 00:14:29.470
But that's rather dull, too.

00:14:30.860 --> 00:14:32.070
You're right.

00:14:33.110 --> 00:14:34.320
Uh, I mean...

00:14:34.320 --> 00:14:37.630
Usually, crossing two negatives 
makes a positive,

00:14:37.630 --> 00:14:40.250
but two dull things don't 
make something fancy...

00:14:40.250 --> 00:14:41.330
Right?

00:14:42.750 --> 00:14:43.590
I apologize.

00:14:44.260 --> 00:14:48.110
We do need a Llama Day and 
we need to really push it.

00:14:48.650 --> 00:14:51.490
Push? What does that mean?

00:14:51.490 --> 00:14:53.260
We have to make it so people will

00:14:53.260 --> 00:14:55.080
be dying to see Mr. Llama, right?

00:14:55.520 --> 00:14:57.390
Let's add some bonus.

00:14:57.970 --> 00:14:59.080
Bonus?

00:14:59.080 --> 00:15:00.760
Like all-you-can-dig-holes.

00:15:01.420 --> 00:15:04.000
I think you'd be the only one 
who'd appreciate that, Badger.

00:15:04.550 --> 00:15:08.140
How about giving out figures 
to only people who visit him?

00:15:08.140 --> 00:15:09.300
A figure of who?

00:15:09.300 --> 00:15:11.390
Of me, of course.

00:15:11.950 --> 00:15:14.410
You'll receive a limited 
edition figure of me

00:15:14.410 --> 00:15:17.170
just for glancing at Mr. Llama.

00:15:17.710 --> 00:15:19.440
I guess I'm just secondary.

00:15:20.010 --> 00:15:23.200
Then how about you get to take 
a commemorative picture

00:15:23.200 --> 00:15:24.560
if you go see Mr. Llama?

00:15:24.560 --> 00:15:25.570
A picture with who?

00:15:25.570 --> 00:15:26.910
With me, of course.

00:15:27.430 --> 00:15:29.450
I'm not really needed there, am I?

00:15:30.630 --> 00:15:33.080
How about everyone takes some

00:15:33.080 --> 00:15:35.980
time to think up ideas for Llama Day?

00:15:35.980 --> 00:15:37.160
I think that's a good idea.

00:15:37.510 --> 00:15:39.390
Agreed!

00:15:37.960 --> 00:15:40.580
Agree—

00:15:40.580 --> 00:15:50.590
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:15:54.690 --> 00:15:56.640
So you had a meeting about that...

00:15:57.190 --> 00:15:59.420
How about you invite a friend

00:15:59.420 --> 00:16:02.030
to do something with you, Mr. Llama?

00:16:02.710 --> 00:16:04.770
Mr. Llama's friend?

00:16:05.580 --> 00:16:07.100
A friend?

00:16:08.970 --> 00:16:11.740
Well, I do like Mr. Alpaca.

00:16:13.360 --> 00:16:15.710
Hey, look at that!

00:16:15.710 --> 00:16:18.200
Oh, how cute!

00:16:18.580 --> 00:16:20.440
Hey, let's take a picture!

00:16:20.440 --> 00:16:22.670
An alpaca. How cute!

00:16:23.170 --> 00:16:25.130
I'm a llama.

00:16:25.130 --> 00:16:26.010
Huh?

00:16:26.670 --> 00:16:28.100
A llama?

00:16:28.100 --> 00:16:30.180
You're not an alpaca?

00:16:30.180 --> 00:16:32.610
Now that you mention it, 
you are different.

00:16:32.610 --> 00:16:34.560
You have long eyelashes, but...

00:16:35.140 --> 00:16:36.180
I apologize.

00:16:36.680 --> 00:16:37.860
Never mind, then.

00:16:37.860 --> 00:16:38.600
Yeah.

00:16:39.910 --> 00:16:42.340
The few people that do 
come to visit me,

00:16:42.340 --> 00:16:44.100
nine times out of ten,

00:16:44.100 --> 00:16:47.360
are there because they 
mistook me for an alpaca.

00:16:47.750 --> 00:16:49.750
You actually get ten people?

00:16:50.360 --> 00:16:52.840
I'm talking about 
probabilities, Panda.

00:16:53.730 --> 00:16:57.740
Then why don't you all 
make a team of camels?

00:16:58.370 --> 00:17:02.110
Maybe they won't be concerned 
with llamas or alpacas then?

00:17:02.110 --> 00:17:05.450
Don't wrap it up so 
easily, Polar Bear!

00:17:05.450 --> 00:17:07.420
They have their own identities!

00:17:08.060 --> 00:17:09.980
Oh, is that so?

00:17:09.980 --> 00:17:12.120
I don't really understand.

00:17:12.120 --> 00:17:15.090
You know, since we're one of a kind.

00:17:16.090 --> 00:17:17.430
You guys...

00:17:17.950 --> 00:17:19.310
It must be nice.

00:17:19.960 --> 00:17:21.650
Neither of you look like anyone else,

00:17:21.650 --> 00:17:24.230
so you're never mistaken 
for someone else.

00:17:24.690 --> 00:17:26.650
Well, since it's troublesome 
to look alike,

00:17:26.650 --> 00:17:29.150
why not highlight some differences?

00:17:29.750 --> 00:17:32.010
Differences? Like color?

00:17:32.010 --> 00:17:36.180
Mr. Llama is brown, 
and Mr. Alpaca is white.

00:17:36.180 --> 00:17:38.520
But there are brown alpacas, too.

00:17:39.260 --> 00:17:41.800
Mr. Alpaca is the popular one.

00:17:41.800 --> 00:17:43.580
Mr. Llama is the dull one.

00:17:44.180 --> 00:17:46.870
I don't think that's 
considered a highlight.

00:17:47.560 --> 00:17:51.390
Then how about highlighting freshness?

00:17:51.850 --> 00:17:52.970
Freshness?

00:17:53.540 --> 00:17:55.620
I think that's a great idea.

00:17:55.620 --> 00:18:00.140
There's a huge difference 
between grapefruit juice

00:18:00.140 --> 00:18:02.310
and fresh grapefruit juice.

00:18:03.270 --> 00:18:05.020
So, fresh llama it is.

00:18:05.020 --> 00:18:15.440
Now Featuring
Fresh Llama

00:18:09.070 --> 00:18:11.590
It almost seems like chilled 
ramen in the summer time.

00:18:12.680 --> 00:18:14.980
What about in the winter?

00:18:15.440 --> 00:18:24.620
Fresh Llama 
Season is Over

00:18:16.520 --> 00:18:17.830
It'll be on break.

00:18:18.910 --> 00:18:23.120
On Break

00:18:19.550 --> 00:18:21.460
I don't think that's a good idea.

00:18:24.620 --> 00:18:28.120
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:18:30.360 --> 00:18:32.510
I've been giving it a lot of thought.

00:18:32.510 --> 00:18:34.090
How about a behavioral display?

00:18:34.870 --> 00:18:36.360
Behavioral display?

00:18:36.360 --> 00:18:39.390
We'll have you act 
like you usually do

00:18:39.390 --> 00:18:41.700
so people can see your natural 
born features and abilities

00:18:41.700 --> 00:18:44.060
as well as how you live.

00:18:44.560 --> 00:18:45.820
Sounds good.

00:18:45.820 --> 00:18:48.560
So you'll be showing 
how Mr. Llama lives.

00:18:49.310 --> 00:18:50.380
How I live?

00:18:50.870 --> 00:18:54.860
We'll have people know exactly 
what kind of llama you are.

00:18:54.860 --> 00:18:58.860
What Exactly Should We Do For Llama Day?

00:18:55.530 --> 00:18:57.050
Sounds great!

00:18:57.050 --> 00:18:58.370
Let's do it!

00:18:58.370 --> 00:19:00.200
We should do everything we can.

00:18:59.520 --> 00:19:01.070
It's Llama Day, right?

00:19:01.070 --> 00:19:02.040
Let's give it our all.

00:19:02.700 --> 00:19:04.790
So exactly what kind of llama are you?

00:19:07.010 --> 00:19:08.750
When I was young...

00:19:09.460 --> 00:19:11.490
I ate a lot of grass.

00:19:14.240 --> 00:19:16.330
And now that I'm big...

00:19:19.150 --> 00:19:20.810
I eat grass.

00:19:23.980 --> 00:19:28.190
I eat... grass, too...

00:19:27.380 --> 00:19:29.100
It's all about the impact.

00:19:29.570 --> 00:19:34.060
How about we all discuss 
how we see Mr. Llama?

00:19:34.710 --> 00:19:37.060
He's more brown than Mr. Alpaca.

00:19:38.150 --> 00:19:40.580
His ears are longer than Mr. Alpaca.

00:19:41.930 --> 00:19:45.030
His eyelashes are about the 
same length as Mr. Alpaca's.

00:19:45.760 --> 00:19:48.450
We didn't mean comparisons 
with Mr. Alpaca.

00:19:49.320 --> 00:19:50.840
He's very courteous.

00:19:51.870 --> 00:19:52.830
He's very quiet.

00:19:53.870 --> 00:19:54.880
He's mature.

00:19:55.790 --> 00:19:56.940
He's calm.

00:19:57.860 --> 00:20:01.550
He... is... po... lite...

00:20:02.940 --> 00:20:06.340
How about something 
that stands out more?

00:20:06.850 --> 00:20:08.610
You don't need to hold 
back, Mr. Llama.

00:20:08.610 --> 00:20:09.980
What do you think?

00:20:10.780 --> 00:20:12.390
Let's see...

00:20:13.580 --> 00:20:17.150
I like to live quietly 
in the mountains.

00:20:19.370 --> 00:20:22.160
Then do we really need a Llama Day?

00:20:22.600 --> 00:20:24.590
I'd like to quietly stand out.

00:20:24.590 --> 00:20:26.460
That's a tad difficult.

00:20:30.410 --> 00:20:32.080
Oh, I just remembered.

00:20:32.960 --> 00:20:35.880
You're really good at 
spitting, aren't you?

00:20:36.480 --> 00:20:38.270
I've sealed away that ability.

00:20:38.270 --> 00:20:40.660
Why not push that angle?

00:20:41.540 --> 00:20:43.300
Well, you see...

00:21:00.410 --> 00:21:03.520
It's not a good idea to 
trouble the customers...

00:21:04.190 --> 00:21:06.240
What about a parade?

00:21:06.490 --> 00:21:09.330
You don't really have to 
do anything, just walk.

00:21:10.130 --> 00:21:12.080
How about a Llamatical Parade?

00:21:14.620 --> 00:21:18.540
Llama

00:21:15.670 --> 00:21:17.170
Where am I?

00:21:19.150 --> 00:21:19.980
Here.

00:21:20.820 --> 00:21:23.950
We could probably do a parade 
even without Mr. Llama.

00:21:26.100 --> 00:21:29.970
If there was only something 
I could be proud of...

00:21:34.470 --> 00:21:36.400
I got it!

00:21:36.400 --> 00:21:40.400
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:21:40.400 --> 00:21:42.860
Today is Llama Day

00:21:44.760 --> 00:21:47.810
I wonder what they actually 
do on Llama Day.

00:21:47.810 --> 00:21:49.830
Well, let's go see.

00:21:50.910 --> 00:21:52.980
Hello. Welcome.

00:21:56.310 --> 00:21:58.750
Huh? Nothing's changed, has it?

00:21:59.280 --> 00:22:02.070
What are you doing for Llama Day?

00:22:02.510 --> 00:22:03.530
It's flourishing.

00:22:03.920 --> 00:22:05.040
What is?

00:22:05.650 --> 00:22:06.970
Right here.

00:22:08.050 --> 00:22:08.990
Here.

00:22:12.430 --> 00:22:13.620
Your eyelashes?

00:22:14.420 --> 00:22:17.030
You're sparkling, Mr. Llama.

00:22:17.390 --> 00:22:24.860
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:23:54.910 --> 00:24:24.830
Next Time

00:23:58.070 --> 00:23:59.710
Mr. Penguin, Mr. Penguin.

00:23:59.710 --> 00:24:00.790
What is it, Panda?

00:24:00.790 --> 00:24:02.500
Where do you think you can get more

00:24:02.500 --> 00:24:04.150
money than you'll ever be able to use?

00:24:04.150 --> 00:24:05.450
I don't think you can.

00:24:05.450 --> 00:24:07.710
Then how about we make 
an annual salary contract

00:24:07.710 --> 00:24:09.220
like a major leaguer?

00:24:09.220 --> 00:24:10.800
I can't think of a reason to make

00:24:10.800 --> 00:24:12.670
an annual salary contract with you.

00:24:12.670 --> 00:24:14.900
Then you can just give 
me an annual salary.

00:24:14.900 --> 00:24:16.260
My major feeling on that

00:24:16.260 --> 00:24:17.280
would be a no.

00:24:17.280 --> 00:24:18.680
Let's end this, Polar Bear.

00:24:18.680 --> 00:24:20.560
Next week's Polar Bear's Café,

00:24:20.560 --> 00:24:21.690
will be presented to you if we can.

00:24:21.690 --> 00:24:22.890
It'll be presented as usual.

00:24:21.830 --> 00:24:24.540
Mr. Penguin's Dilemma
Idol: Yama Arashi

00:24:22.890 --> 00:24:24.730
Enjoy!
